lines+=['','Full failure summaries and every state occurrence are in data/axe.json and data/deduplicated-findings.json. Axe incomplete color checks are not passes.','', '## Text, focus, touch and motion','', f"{len(small)} deduplicated small-text/touch-type observations and {len(targets)} sub-44px target candidates are in data/deduplicated-findings.json. Some are nested SVG drawings rather than actual hit areas: inspect the enclosing button before treating as a touch failure.", '', 'Tab traversal samples, active labels, outline and shadow are in data/focus.json. Focus screenshots show the endpoint, not every focused element. A missing outline may have a box-shadow alternative; weak/missing rings require comparison against neighbors. Reduced-motion screenshots verify a rendering state, not vestibular safety or measured frame rate. Hover companions cover captured controls; not every icon animation is independently performance-tested.','', '## Design improvements - quick wins','', '1. Restore contrast through shared light-theme muted/secondary and input-placeholder tokens using measured failures above. Keep Inter, existing hierarchy and true-black dark canvas. Expected effect: labels, source pills and status copy readable without redesign.', '2. Give necessary input/control borders >=3:1 contrast. Use the boundary proposal above, with explicit hover/selected geometry or icon/text confirmation rather than relying on small surface shifts. Expected effect: forms and selected references become distinguishable.', '3. Make keyboard focus visible on textarea/input and every icon action: proposed `2px solid #91d7ff` dark and `2px solid #215a7b` light, offset 3px; validate contrast against each local neighbor. Keep pointer-focus suppression where approved. Expected effect: reliable keyboard location.', '4. At touch widths raise prose below 16px to 16px/1.5 and metadata below 12px to 12px/1.4. Use 44px minimum enclosing button hit areas, not enlarged SVG drawings. Expected effect: fewer tiny labels and mistaps.', '5. Bring the repair worksheet into the first useful reading viewport by collapsing repeated lesson explanation above it (proposed 16px top gap and an accessible View lesson disclosure). See repair screenshots. Keep equation lining numerals/shared baseline and crimson annotation unchanged.', '', '## Larger improvements','', '- Consolidate source/context/lesson metadata into a consistent semantic row and maintain H1 -> H2 hierarchy; axe heading findings identify exact screens.', '- Review focus restoration and hidden/inert controls across modal/panel transitions. Keep closing path and origin consistent; respect reduced motion without removing feedback.', '- Use local announced waiting/error rows; preserve text + icon for errors and Step/Check this sign for equation annotation. Those labels help avoid color-only meaning. Selected/active states and hover need semantic state checks beyond numerical color deltas.', '- Add a deliberately long-content and 200% zoom follow-up audit; do not infer robust truncation/reflow from these short synthetic fixtures.', '', '## Owner decisions to reconsider','', '- The full first-screen Home divider/spacing is owner-approved V09. At 360x640 it may add scrolling and dilute density; do not remove it without approval. Compare home-360 screenshots.', '- True black and one translucent material are retained. Do not solve weak control separation by adding stacked glass or a new decorative palette.', '- Crimson equation annotation, icy-blue accents, orange Submit, green Save and colored format/image icons reflect existing owner decisions. Contrast can be corrected without replacing those meanings. List weak combinations as proposals, not applied redesign.', '', '## Proposed token table - implementation follow-up only','', '| Scope | Old value/source | Dark proposal | Light proposal | Rationale |','|---|---|---|---|---|','| Primary ink | See computed per-screen tokens in contrast.json | #ffffff | #16181b | Preserve neutral readable body |','| Muted text | Measured failing muted pairs | #b8c0cc | #525866 | Raise secondary-text contrast on base/surfaces |','| Faint/placeholder | Measured failing placeholder pairs | #a9b2c0 at opacity 1 | #62656c at opacity 1 | Avoid compounded alpha |','| Required control border | Measured border/surface candidates | #89919d | #767676 | Target >=3:1; check both sides |','| Keyboard ring | Per-control computed outline/shadow | #91d7ff, 2px, offset 3px | #215a7b, 2px, offset 3px | Separate pointer and keyboard states |','| Touch prose/metadata | Size entries in findings JSON | 16px/1.5 and min12px metadata | Same | Readability at 390/360 widths |','', 'Exact old RGB values and passing per-backdrop replacement ratios appear in the failure table. This table is a proposed mapping, not evidence that a global replacement passes every material.','', '### Follow-up prompt','', '> Implement only the confirmed readability fixes from this report after reading the three handoff documents and actual cascade. Preserve V01-V09 and owner colors/materials. Start with light-theme foreground/placeholder contrast, required control boundaries, keyboard rings and touch type. Use the measured old -> proposed foreground pairs and rerun the state matrix; do not apply candidate surface warnings blindly or alter unrelated backend behavior.', '', '## Not verified / limitations','', '- No real model, account, Google/OAuth, transcription, OCR or external network integrations; fixture response quality is not AI quality.', '- No real touch device/virtual keyboard, screen reader, OS forced colors, zoom or comprehensive color-blindness simulation.', '- Gradient/notebook text-over-art and blurred overlapping materials need pixel-level sampling; ancestor compositing alone cannot certify them.', '- Color-only conveyance requires manual semantic review. Error and equation annotation have text labels; untested icon/selected states are not certified.', '- See data/browser-errors.json and rows marked INCOMPLETE for capture or walkthrough gaps. Videos are deterministic fixture evidence and must not be described as a clean completed workflow if a walkthrough error is recorded.', '- Attachment chips, export icons and worksheets only count as captured if their actual selectors/content appear; absent states remain gaps rather than simulated pixels.', '', '## Process and preservation proof','', 'See data/git-status-before.txt, data/git-status-after.txt, data/preservation.json and data/cleanup.json. Existing workspace changes predate this audit. Only the new .ui_review evidence directory is allowed to differ.']
